def isMatch(s, p):
    m, n = len(s), len(p)
    dp = [[False] * (n + 1) for _ in range(m + 1)]
    dp[0][0] = True
    # '*' can match empty sequence
    for j in range(1, n + 1):
        if p[j-1] == '*':
            dp[0][j] = dp[0][j-1]
    for i in range(1, m + 1):
        for j in range(1, n + 1):
            if p[j-1] == '*':
                # '*' matches empty (dp[i][j-1])
                # or one more char (dp[i-1][j])
                dp[i][j] = dp[i][j-1] or dp[i-1][j]
            elif p[j-1] == '?' or p[j-1] == s[i-1]:
                dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1]
    return dp[m][n]
`

**Complexity:** $O(mn)$ time and space where $m = |s|$, $n = |p|$. The key recurrence for '*' is that it either matches zero characters (look left) or one more character (look up).

